From 387be34dd722c74e6576d6e94d92ae2bffe14660 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arealjim <6187715+arealjim@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 23:01:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 47/48] runtime: stream the app's depth to the client as a
 small grid (positional reprojection)

With depth_grid > 0 (default 64) the runtime advertises
XR_KHR_composition_layer_depth. When a Vulkan depth swapchain image is
released, depth_grid evenly spaced full-width rows are copied to a host
buffer (a ring of fenced slots). xrEndFrame picks up each view's
XrCompositionLayerDepthInfoKHR; the encode thread reduces the captured rows
to a grid x grid inverse-distance image per eye (q = 255 * 0.25 m / z, 0 =
infinitely far; standard, reversed and infinite Z), waiting at most 4 ms for
the copy. Grids go only to a client that set CLIENT_CAPABILITY_DEPTH_GRID:
on Wi-Fi as datagrams flagged as render poses whose payload starts with a
DepthGridHeader, on USB as TcpRecordType::DepthGrid records.
